{number: 121}
{title: O for a Thousand Tongues}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [G] for a thousand [C] tongues to [G] sing
My [C] great Re-[G] deemer's [D7] praise,
The [G] glories of my [C] God and [G] King,
The [C] triumphs [G] of His [D7] [G] grace!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
My [G] gracious Master [C] and my [G] God,
As-[C] sist me [G] to pro-[D7] claim,
To [G] spread through all the [C] earth a-[G] broad
The [C] honors [G] of Thy [D7] [G] name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Jesus! the name that [C] charms our [G] fears,
That [C] bids our [G] sorrows [D7] cease;
'Tis [G] music in the [C] sinner's [G] ears,
'Tis [C] life, and [G] health, and [D7] [G] peace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
He [G] breaks the pow'r of [C] canceled [G] sin,
He [C] sets the [G] pris'ner [D7] free;
His [G] blood can make the [C] foulest [G] clean,
His [C] blood a-[G] vailed for [D7] [G] me.
{end_of_verse}
